---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PUBLIC_SITE_URL } from 'astro:env/client';

const seoTitle = 'Best Dream11 Alternatives in India 2026: Top Gaming Apps Compared';
const seoDescription =
	'Comprehensive guide to the best Dream11 alternatives in India 2026 — comparing Comegame, MPL, My11Circle, PlayerzPot, Gamezy, and more on features, safety, and usability.';
const canonicalUrl = `${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/blog/best-dream11-alternatives-india-comegame`;
const ogImage = `${PUBLIC_SITE_URL}/android-chrome-512x512.png`;
const keywordsMeta =
	'best dream11 alternatives india 2026, apps like dream11, comegame vs dream11, mpl vs dream11, my11circle, playzerpot, gamezy, vision11, online gaming apps india';

const articleSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'BlogPosting',
	headline: seoTitle,
	description: seoDescription,
	url: canonicalUrl,
	image: ogImage,
	datePublished: '2026-03-24',
	dateModified: '2026-07-02',
	inLanguage: 'en-IN',
	author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Come Game Guide' },
	publisher: {
		'@type': 'Organization',
		name: 'Come Game Guide',
		logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: ogImage },
	},
	mainEntityOfPage: canonicalUrl,
};

const faqSchema = {
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'FAQPage',
	mainEntity: [
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Which is the best Dream11 alternative in India in 2026?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'There is no single best alternative — it depends on your goals. My11Circle suits fantasy sports fans, MPL suits variety seekers, and Comegame suits beginners who want a simpler skill-game environment.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Is Comegame safe to use in India?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Comegame follows standard KYC and data security practices. Always verify your account and read the platform terms before depositing. Check state-specific laws before participating in real-money formats.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Are Dream11 alternatives legal in India?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Most fantasy and skill-game platforms operate under the skill-game legal framework in India, but laws vary by state. Always verify your local regulations before using any real-money platform.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Can I use multiple gaming platforms at the same time?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'Yes, you can have accounts on multiple platforms. However, managing bankroll and time across several apps requires discipline — spread too thin, and you may not perform well on any of them.',
			},
		},
		{
			'@type': 'Question',
			name: 'Which platform is best for beginners switching from Dream11?',
			acceptedAnswer: {
				'@type': 'Answer',
				text: 'For beginners, Comegame and Vision11 are generally recommended because of their simpler interfaces and lower-complexity onboarding. My11Circle is a good choice if you want a familiar fantasy-sports format.',
			},
		},
	],
};
---

<Layout
	title={seoTitle}
	description={seoDescription}
	keywords={keywordsMeta}
	canonical={canonicalUrl}
	ogImage={ogImage}
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)}></script>
		<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)}></script>
	</Fragment>

	<article class="container mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
		<header class="max-w-4xl">
			<a href="/blog" class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-border bg-card px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
				Back to Blog
			</a>
			<h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-5xl">
				Best Dream11 Alternatives in India 2026: Top Gaming Apps Compared
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-muted-foreground">Published on March 24, 2026 | Updated July 2, 2026 | Comparison Guide | 12 min read</p>
			<p class="mt-5 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground md:text-lg">
				Dream11 built the fantasy gaming habit for millions of Indian users. But by 2026, a much wider
				ecosystem of platforms competes for the same audience — and many users are actively looking for
				something different. Whether the reason is interface fatigue, game format variety, bonus
				structures, or simply curiosity, switching to or supplementing Dream11 with another platform
				is now a common decision. This guide covers every major contender with honest, comparable
				depth so you can choose based on facts rather than marketing.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="mt-8 max-w-5xl overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card/50 p-5">
			<div class="grid items-center gap-4 md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr]">
				<img src="/logo.svg" alt="Best Dream11 alternatives India 2026 comparison guide" class="h-16 w-16 rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-2" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
				<p class="text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
					Quick summary: this guide compares My11Circle, MPL, Gamezy, PlayerzPot, Vision11, and
					<a href="/come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame</a> across features, safety, bonuses, and fit for different user types.
					Read our <a href="/responsible-gaming" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">responsible gaming guide</a> before joining any platform.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<section class="mt-10 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Why Indian Users Are Seeking Dream11 Alternatives in 2026</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Dream11 is undeniably the largest fantasy gaming brand in India. It has IPL sponsorships, a
				massive user base, and strong brand recognition. But size and dominance do not automatically
				translate to the best experience for every type of user. Over the past two years, several
				specific frustrations have driven significant user migration away from Dream11 — not necessarily
				permanent departures, but supplementary exploration of what else the market offers.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The first major driver is regulatory change. India's gaming regulations have evolved significantly,
				with TDS (Tax Deducted at Source) rules applying to winnings above certain thresholds and
				several states tightening their stance on real-money gaming. These changes affected all platforms,
				but Dream11's large user base made the friction more visible. Users who experienced withdrawal
				complications or tax-related confusion began researching platforms that might offer clearer,
				more transparent processes. If you are navigating these questions, our <a href="/faq" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">FAQ section</a> addresses
				the most common legal and financial queries about online gaming in India.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The second driver is UX fatigue. Dream11's interface is dense — tournament selection, team
				creation across multiple sports, contest entry, live score tracking, and promotion management
				all compete for screen space. Users who want a simpler, faster experience have found that newer
				platforms like <a href="/come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame</a> and Vision11 offer cleaner flows without the cognitive
				overhead. This matters especially for users who play casually and do not need the full feature
				set Dream11 provides.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The third driver is game variety. Dream11 is fundamentally a fantasy sports platform. If you
				want skill games, card games, arcade challenges, or non-sports game types, Dream11 does not serve
				you. Platforms like MPL and Comegame fill this gap directly. The growing appetite for diverse
				digital gaming — not just sports prediction — has created real demand for alternatives with
				broader game libraries.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">What to Look for When Choosing a Gaming Platform</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Before reviewing each platform, it helps to establish evaluation criteria. Without a framework,
				comparisons become subjective and misleading. Here are the six dimensions that matter most for
				Indian users choosing between gaming apps in 2026.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Game variety and format fit:</strong> Does the platform offer the
				game types you actually want to play? A fantasy-only platform is useless to someone who wants
				skill-based card games. Inventory your actual preferences before comparing.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Onboarding complexity:</strong> How quickly can a new user go
				from download to first match? Platforms with complex KYC upfront, multi-step tutorials, or
				confusing navigation create early drop-off. Simpler onboarding reduces the learning tax,
				especially for users switching from another platform. Our guide on
				<a href="/blog/how-comegame-works-features-gameplay-basics" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">how Comegame works</a>
				shows what smooth onboarding looks like in practice.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Payment and withdrawal reliability:</strong> This is where
				platforms most commonly disappoint users. Check community reviews specifically on withdrawal
				speed, minimum withdrawal thresholds, and whether UPI transfers work smoothly. Slow
				withdrawals are the single most consistent complaint across gaming platforms in India.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Bonus transparency:</strong> Welcome bonuses are marketing tools.
				What matters is the wagering requirement — how many times you must play through the bonus
				amount before it becomes withdrawable. High wagering requirements (20x or above) effectively
				make bonuses worthless for casual users. Always read bonus terms before claiming.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Legal standing and safety record:</strong> Is the platform
				operating legally in your state? Does it have a credible KYC process? A platform that skips
				identity verification may seem convenient upfront but creates real problems during withdrawals
				or disputes. We cover this in more detail in the legal section below.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Responsible gaming tools:</strong> Does the platform offer
				deposit limits, session timers, or self-exclusion options? This matters more than most users
				realize until they need it. Any platform worth using long-term should have these features
				built in. Visit our <a href="/responsible-gaming" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">responsible gaming page</a>
				for a full breakdown of what good responsible gaming tools look like.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">My11Circle — Full Overview</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				My11Circle is the most structurally similar alternative to Dream11. Both platforms are built
				around fantasy cricket, and the core gameplay loop — selecting players, building a team, joining
				a contest, tracking live scores — is nearly identical. This makes My11Circle the default
				recommendation for Dream11 users who want a familiar format with a different platform experience.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The platform's key differentiator historically has been its promotion of player freedom in team
				selection. While Dream11 uses its own scoring algorithm that sometimes penalizes unconventional
				picks, My11Circle's early positioning was around giving users more control over their selection
				strategies. In practice, the difference is marginal for casual users but noticeable for
				experienced fantasy players who have strong independent analysis methods.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				My11Circle suits users who: are deeply invested in cricket fantasy, have an existing selection
				methodology they want to test on a different scoring system, and want a clean UI with familiar
				contest formats. It is not ideal for users seeking game variety outside fantasy sports. For
				those users, platforms like MPL or <a href="/come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame</a> are more appropriate.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">MPL (Mobile Premier League) — Full Overview</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				MPL is one of the broadest gaming platforms in India. Where Dream11 and My11Circle are
				fantasy-sports-focused, MPL spans fantasy cricket, casual mobile games, arcade-style skill games,
				chess, carrom, and more. This breadth makes MPL genuinely different from Dream11 — it is less
				a direct alternative and more of a different product category: a multi-format gaming app rather
				than a pure fantasy platform.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				MPL's strength is its variety. The platform lets users switch between game types in a single
				session without needing separate apps. This appeals to users who want options without
				juggling multiple logins. The downside is that this variety comes with interface complexity —
				MPL's dashboard is busier than most competitors, and newer users often report confusion during
				their first few sessions. Our guide to
				<a href="/blog/how-online-gaming-platforms-like-comegame-operate" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">how online gaming platforms operate</a>
				explains why multi-format platforms tend to have more complex interfaces than single-format ones.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				MPL suits users who want variety above all else, are comfortable with a learning curve on a new
				platform, and plan to play multiple game types regularly. It is less ideal for users who want
				one game format done simply and quickly.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Gamezy — Overview</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Gamezy positions itself as a fantasy sports platform with a particular strength in regional
				language support and accessibility for users outside major metros. It offers cricket, football,
				kabaddi, and basketball fantasy formats — a lineup that directly competes with Dream11's core
				offering but with added attention to localization.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				One aspect that Gamezy users frequently highlight is contest size management. The platform
				tends to offer more small-to-medium contests relative to its large-tournament options, which
				statistically gives individual users better winning odds than Dream11's mega contests with
				millions of participants. For users frustrated by consistently missing Dream11 top prizes
				despite solid team selections, Gamezy's smaller pool structure can feel like a genuine
				upgrade in playability. This kind of platform-by-platform comparison is also covered in
				our <a href="/blog/comegame-vs-other-online-gaming-platforms" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame vs other platforms analysis</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">PlayerzPot — Overview</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				PlayerzPot is a multi-sport fantasy platform covering cricket, football, basketball, kabaddi,
				volleyball, and baseball — one of the broadest sport selections among Indian fantasy apps.
				This makes it particularly relevant for users whose sporting interests extend beyond cricket,
				which remains the core focus of Dream11 and My11Circle.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The platform's UX is clean and functional. Onboarding is relatively smooth, and the contest
				lobby is well-organized by sport and match. PlayerzPot has invested in its referral and
				loyalty programs more than some competitors, which makes it appealing for users who plan
				to invite friends or maintain long-term engagement. The withdrawal process has been generally
				well-reviewed in community forums, with UPI transfers typically completing within expected
				timelines — a key practical concern that our
				<a href="/real-money-come-games" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">real money gaming overview</a>
				addresses for all platforms.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Vision11 — Overview</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Vision11 occupies a specific niche: it is consistently recommended as one of the most
				beginner-friendly fantasy platforms in India. The contest structures are simpler, the
				entry fee tiers start lower, and the interface prioritizes clarity over feature density.
				For users who feel overwhelmed by Dream11's competitive ecosystem but still want fantasy
				sports formats, Vision11 is a comfortable entry point.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Vision11's limitation is depth. Power users who want advanced analytics, deep contest
				variety, or high-value prize pools will find Vision11 underwhelming after initial
				exploration. It serves best as either a starting platform for beginners or a supplementary
				platform for experienced users who want a lower-pressure environment on certain match days.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Comegame — Detailed Overview as an Emerging Alternative</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame occupies a distinct position in this comparison because it is not primarily a
				fantasy sports platform. While the platforms above compete directly in the fantasy sports
				segment, Comegame is built around skill-based digital games with a strong emphasis on
				accessible, clean design for Indian users. This makes it a genuinely different type of
				Dream11 alternative — not a replacement for fantasy sports, but a parallel option for users
				who want skill-game experiences outside the sports-prediction format.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The platform's beginner-friendly approach is its most frequently cited strength. Where MPL
				can overwhelm new users with its variety, Comegame's interface prioritizes clarity and fast
				navigation. A first-time user can go from account creation to first match in under ten
				minutes without needing a tutorial. This is a meaningful differentiator in a market where
				most platforms assume users arrive with existing gaming experience. For a full walkthrough,
				visit our <a href="/blog/how-comegame-works-features-gameplay-basics" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">detailed Comegame features and gameplay guide</a>.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Comegame's skill-game focus also addresses a core frustration with fantasy sports platforms:
				the outcomes of fantasy contests depend partially on real-world sports events that no player
				controls. A batsman getting injured mid-innings can derail a perfectly constructed Dream11
				team. On Comegame, outcomes are determined by player decisions within the game itself — no
				external events can invalidate a carefully made choice. This is a fundamentally different
				risk profile that appeals to users who prefer their results to reflect their own decisions
				rather than sporting luck.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				The platform also supports both free and paid game modes, meaning users can practice
				extensively before committing real money. This free-play-first approach is strongly
				aligned with responsible gaming principles — something we explore in full on our
				<a href="/responsible-gaming" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">responsible gaming page</a>.
				Users new to Comegame should spend their first several sessions in free modes, building
				familiarity with game mechanics before entering any paid contests.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				For users considering downloading the app, our
				<a href="/download-come-games-app" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame app download guide</a>
				covers the safest installation process, APK source verification, and device compatibility.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Head-to-Head Comparison Across Six Dimensions</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Rather than presenting a table — which flattens important nuance — this section walks through
				each dimension in narrative form so you can apply the analysis to your own situation.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Game variety:</strong> MPL leads the market on raw game count,
				followed by PlayerzPot on sport variety. Dream11, My11Circle, Gamezy, and Vision11 are all
				primarily fantasy sports platforms with limited format diversity. Comegame stands apart by
				offering skill-based digital game formats that do not exist on fantasy sports platforms at all.
				If variety means "more sports," MPL or PlayerzPot wins. If variety means "different types of
				games entirely," Comegame is the answer.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Onboarding simplicity:</strong> Vision11 and Comegame lead on
				onboarding simplicity. Both minimize required steps and front-load the simplest experience.
				Dream11, despite being the most familiar brand, actually has one of the steeper onboarding
				curves because its team-selection process requires sports knowledge to execute effectively.
				MPL's variety creates onboarding confusion. My11Circle and PlayerzPot are moderate — familiar
				enough to existing fantasy users but not particularly accessible to complete newcomers.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Mobile performance:</strong> All six platforms are mobile-first.
				The differences come in performance on mid-range devices and poor network conditions. Comegame
				and Vision11 have smaller feature sets, which generally means faster load times and less battery
				drain. MPL's large game library comes with higher app size and occasional performance issues
				on older devices. Dream11 is well-optimized but still heavier than simpler alternatives.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Community and user base size:</strong> Dream11 is the clear leader,
				followed by MPL. A larger user base means more contest participants — which translates to larger
				prize pools but also harder competition and lower individual win probability in large-pool contests.
				Smaller platforms like Vision11 and Comegame have fewer participants per contest, which improves
				individual odds but reduces maximum prize sizes. This trade-off is significant and should factor
				into platform choice based on your goals.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Customer support quality:</strong> This is where all platforms have
				room to improve. Dream11 has the most support infrastructure given its scale, but resolution
				times are inconsistent. Smaller platforms may respond faster but have less sophisticated support
				systems. Before depositing significant amounts on any platform, test the support responsiveness
				with a low-stakes query. Our <a href="/faq" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">FAQ page</a>
				covers the most common platform support scenarios with practical guidance.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				<strong class="text-foreground">Skill vs. luck balance:</strong> Fantasy sports platforms sit in
				a hybrid zone — team selection is skill-based, but player performance is luck-based. Comegame's
				skill game formats shift the balance more toward player decision-making. If you want outcomes
				that more directly reflect your own choices and skill development, non-fantasy skill-game
				platforms are the right direction. For a deeper analysis of this distinction, read our
				<a href="/blog/comegame-vs-other-online-gaming-platforms" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame vs other platforms comparison</a>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="mt-8 max-w-4xl rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6">
			<h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Bonus and Promotion Structures</h2>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Welcome bonuses are the primary marketing tool every gaming platform uses to acquire new users,
				and they all look more generous than they actually are in practice. Understanding the mechanics
				behind bonus offers prevents disappointment and misplaced expectations.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Most platforms offer a welcome bonus that matches your first deposit up to a certain amount.
				The key question is always the wagering requirement — how many times you must play through
				the bonus before it becomes eligible for withdrawal. A ₹500 bonus with a 20x wagering
				requirement means you need to generate ₹10,000 in gameplay before you can withdraw the
				bonus funds. For casual users who deposit small amounts and play occasionally, this requirement
				may never be met, effectively making the bonus zero value.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Referral bonuses are generally better value than welcome bonuses because they tend to have
				lower or zero wagering requirements. Every platform in this comparison offers some form of
				referral reward. If you are going to join a new platform, get your referral link set up before
				inviting friends — it benefits both parties. The
				<a href="/" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Comegame homepage</a>
				provides an overview of current promotional offers and how to evaluate them honestly.
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-base leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
				Seasonal and event-based promotions — IPL special contests, festival bonuses, anniversary offers —
